Job-Description:
**Job title**
F5 Traffic Management Sr. Engineer

**Job Summary**
The F5 Traffic Management Sr. Engineer will play a key role in maintaining, configuring, and troubleshooting our client's core networking equipment. They will manage network switches, ISR routers and ensure their configuration meets organizational performance objectives or standards.

**Required Skills**
- In-depth knowledge and hands-on experience with switches, namely Catalyst Switches and ISR routers;
- Proficient in DNS and DHCP;
- Coming with a thorough familiarity with routing protocols such as BGP and EIGRP;
- Proficient in implementing and troubleshoot quality of services (QoS).

**Required Experience**
- At least one year of work experience as a F5 Traffic Management Sr. Engineer;
- Four years spent performing the duties of a Sr. Network Engineer Consultant in Corporate Global Technology settings.

**Responsibilities**
- Engage in stable, performance-oriented and cost-effective network solutions;
- Troubleshoot Cisco routers and switches along other network devices;
- Administer DNS and DHCP;
- Implement and maintain quality of service (QoS) and prioritize network traffic to reduce downtime.

